# What must never enter the build context.
#
# The first block is the important one: a .env copied into a layer stays in the
# image even if a later layer deletes it, and `docker history` will show it.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output and caches — regenerated inside the image, and copying them in
# would let a stale host build shadow the fresh one.
.next
node_modules
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and tooling.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Large artefacts that the running application does not read.
evidence
datasets
docs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Local-only files.
#
# benchmark-tasks.json is NOT here on purpose. RunPanel.tsx imports it
# directly ("../../../benchmark-tasks.json"), so it is a build input: excluding
# it from the build context makes `next build` fail inside the image on module
# resolution while working perfectly on a developer's machine, where the file
# is simply present. device-profile.json has no importer and stays excluded.
device-profile.json
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
README.md
